# Line endings are LF everywhere, including in the working tree on
# Windows.
#
# Without this, git's core.autocrlf rewrites files to CRLF on checkout
# while storing them as LF, and Prettier — which expects LF — then reports
# every file in the repo as badly formatted on a Windows machine while
# passing on CI's Linux runner. The same `npm run format:check` has to
# give the same answer on both, or nobody trusts it.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary files and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
